back between the two.

00:53:05.730 --> 00:53:09.090
So this one is a little
hump, and then way down.

00:53:09.090 --> 00:53:11.402
This one gives you a
little bit more lift,

00:53:11.402 --> 00:53:13.110
but again, perhaps we
could add some more

00:53:13.110 --> 00:53:14.040
features in the model.

00:53:14.040 --> 00:53:16.610
And machine learning is
an iterative process.

00:53:16.610 --> 00:53:18.360
You've got to be
comfortable with failure.

00:53:18.360 --> 00:53:20.310
That's essentially
how a model works.

00:53:20.310 --> 00:53:21.600
It says, all right.

00:53:21.600 --> 00:53:22.890
I know this for the past.

00:53:22.890 --> 00:53:24.540
Here are my inputs.

00:53:24.540 --> 00:53:26.190
Am I going to get
a good result based

00:53:26.190 --> 00:53:29.130
on running this over a
million records or not?

00:53:29.130 --> 00:53:31.680
So it essentially-- and what
the process is called gradient

00:53:31.680 --> 00:53:32.400
descent--

00:53:32.400 --> 00:53:35.270
it will fail, fail, fail,
fail, fail until it gets

00:53:35.270 --> 00:53:36.930
to a point where, OK, cool.

00:53:36.930 --> 00:53:40.440
I think I've modeled the
behavior of one of these users

00:53:40.440 --> 00:53:41.670
effectively.

00:53:41.670 --> 00:53:44.400
So you've done exactly all
the steps a machine learning

00:53:44.400 --> 00:53:46.230
